A few comments on what you wrote. First of all I didn't say anything
about "excitement" (is Sokoban "exciting"? - no it isn't), that's not
the point. Can that get exciting? Sure it can. Because you cannot just
run (teleport/dig) through the level, so any appearing "known problem"
can increase the threat to a degree you have not had before.

> and only adds annoyance and tedium.

Maybe, maybe not. You haven't written much to support your view.

> (And people could stock on c!oGL.)

The c!oGL is hardly an issue at all; first of all the potions are not
the most common, especially on your way down you would at that point
not likely have a "stock" of them, maybe not even one, YMMV. Then your
suggestion would only help in the up-direction (you still have to pass
the level), so I have to assume that you meant that potion just as an
escape scenario in case that monsters pressurise you; in that case
there's the more common cursed/confused teleport available as escape
means (which is also a standard way to bypass *any* non-teleport or
non-dig level), so that's no point against it, either.

> Where's the threat that has you watch out for your life?

Such a "non-run level" can increase the threat of the already existing
features; it could (in a simple way) give a bit pepper to the mid-game.
Not that it would change the game in any fundamental way, I don't want
that, but it would add some detail.[*]

That idea is not meant to be a "threat for your life" by itself; if
you want a new threat of that kind you could just add Nyarlathotep or
any other threatening monster - which is not what I'd suggest.

My first thought about such special trap-rooms was more about atmosphere
than about excitement, but I am also sure that such special rooms will
add some excitement, that they can make a standard situation "just pass
the room" to occasionally become a problem to be solved.[**]

[*] You may want to compare it to the muddy rooms in Nethack; are they
a threat? I think those swamps could be made more interesting as well
simply by not supporting it to circumvent/ignore them completely; the
same non-digging/no-teleport property could support that effect.

[**] It by far no unsolvable problem, but that's not the point.

